Priority order (this matters)

we need to do this in order:

Global exception translator
Missing body / malformed JSON
Validation errors
Catch-all fallback
Business exceptions (as features are added)
{
The 5 categories that cover ~95% of cases
In real production apps, teams usually translate only these:

1)Bad request shape
Missing body
Malformed JSON

2) Validation failures
@NotNull, @Size, etc.

3) Type mismatches
Wrong param types

4) Resource not found
Invalid IDs
Wrong URLs

5) Unexpected server errors
Null pointers
Bugs
}
What may be needed to be implemented (minimum)

1 Global exception translator
→ One place that converts any error in ErrorResponse

2 Handle framework request errors
→ Missing body, bad JSON, validation errors
→ These happen before controller methods

3 Small error-code set
→ BAD_REQUEST, VALIDATION_ERROR, UNAUTHORIZED, NOT_FOUND, INTERNAL_ERROR

4 Catch-all fallback
→ For unexpected server bugs
→ Always returns a safe, consistent error

